// spec: a compile server's builds after a function's string literal is changed and after a function with a literal of its own is removed are what a build from scratch gives, in every configuration: the module keeps no literal its texts no longer name (until 2026-11-22 a release build's server kept the old literal, and --verify-incremental found "what it wrote differs")
//--- step: the program
[[maybe_unused]] void extra() { std::println("a literal of its own"); }

int main()
{
  std::println("first literal");
  return 0;
}
// expect: first literal
//--- step: the literal changed
[[maybe_unused]] void extra() { std::println("a literal of its own"); }

int main()
{
  std::println("second literal");
  return 0;
}
// expect: second literal
//--- step: the function with its own literal removed
int main()
{
  std::println("second literal");
  return 0;
}
// expect: second literal
